WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.468
-Thank you.
So great to see you again,

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.670
because we got to start
off the week together.

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:07.573
-We did, yeah.
-You went to the Met Gala.

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:11.411
And here's a photo of you here.
Look at this.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.979
Stunner.
Looking gorgeous in...

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:14.880
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.084
-Thank you.
-...gorgeous in Thom Browne.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.186
We sat at the same table.
-Yeah.

00:00:20.186 --> 00:00:22.154
-We were taping.
-I had a great time with you.

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:23.489
-We did, right?
We had fun.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:26.425
-Yeah, I feel like I had
the Met Gala with Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:26.425 --> 00:00:28.994
It was the best experience
I could have had.

00:00:28.994 --> 00:00:30.396
You were cracking me up
the whole time.

00:00:30.396 --> 00:00:32.965
-I want to talk to you
about "Dear Evan Hansen,"

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:37.370
but I also want to talk to you
about your musical abilities.

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:40.073
You can -- You can sing.
-Wow. Thanks.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:45.278
-I mean, would you -- would you
ever put out music as you?

00:00:45.278 --> 00:00:48.180
-Totally, yeah.
I'm en route to that,

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:49.515
into releasing music.

00:00:49.515 --> 00:00:51.484
-Do you record anything?
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.421
Yeah, I have
a single droppin' soon.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:00:57.456
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Wait. What?

00:00:57.456 --> 00:00:58.891
Really?
That's fantastic.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.693
And how does it --
Do you get nervous when you --

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.328
when you do these things,
and you're like --

00:01:02.328 --> 00:01:04.096
'Cause, like, I watched
this movie, and I'm like,

00:01:04.096 --> 00:01:06.532
"Oh, if I even did
one scene of that --"

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:07.800
I can do it joking around,

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:10.637
but really singing in front
of all these people

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:13.940
and Ben Platt, as well,
I go, "Oof."

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.608
-Oh, yeah, I was so nervous.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.311
Yeah, 'cause I come from film,
you know, so I wasn't --

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:22.148
Like, I'm not well-versed
in the world of musical theater.

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.649
In my scene in particular,

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:24.950
I remember talking
to Kaitlyn Dever

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.120
before we shot the film
and being like,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:29.855
"I'm really nervous
to sing in front of people."

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.091
And she was like, "Don't worry.
It's gonna be chill.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:35.427
Most of the scenes take place
in bedrooms and hallways,

00:01:35.427 --> 00:01:38.364
and it's very intimate."
And I remember thinking,

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.667
"Okay, cool."
And then, Stephen Chbosky,

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.535
our director,
calls me and is like,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.403
"So, your scene's
gonna take place

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:47.606
during an all-school assembly."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.606 --> 00:01:49.042
-The most people in any scene
in the whole movie.

00:01:49.042 --> 00:01:53.646
-Yes, an all-school assembly.
150 people are watching you.

00:01:53.646 --> 00:01:54.713
-150 people there.

00:01:54.713 --> 00:01:57.517
Yeah.
So, you know, we get to the day,

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:00.219
and I perform the scene,
and it goes well and everything.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:02.589
And then, at the end of the day,
the sound guys are like,

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:07.026
"We really need to get a clean
vocal tracking of the song,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:09.595
so what we're gonna have
everyone do

00:02:09.595 --> 00:02:11.964
is get in a large circle,

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:14.968
and we're gonna put you
in the middle of the circle,

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:18.805
and then you're gonna perform
the entire song a cappella."

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.573
[ Laughter ]
-That's a nightmare.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:24.477
-There was, like,
this demon ring of human beings,

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:27.313
like 150 people
just in dead silence,

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:29.581
like, staring at me
while I performed the song.

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:30.750
But they were all really lovely

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.618
and also, like, fans
of "Dear Evan Hansen,"

00:02:32.618 --> 00:02:36.556
so it went all right.
-But they added two new songs

00:02:36.556 --> 00:02:38.891
to the soundtrack
for this film adaptation,

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.994
and you're one of the songs.
-Yeah.

00:02:40.994 --> 00:02:44.263
-Congrats on that.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.231
It's fantastic.
It's a beautiful song,

00:02:46.231 --> 00:02:47.667
"The Anonymous Ones."

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:50.302
And you actually got to write
it, as well, or co-write it?

00:02:50.302 --> 00:02:53.306
-Yeah, I did. Yeah.
I co-wrote it

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.174
with Benj Pasek and Justin Paul.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.343
-The guys, the dudes.
-The dudes!

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.178
Those dudes rock.
-Fantastic.

00:02:59.178 --> 00:03:02.782
I mean, "La La Land,"
"The Greatest Showman."

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.550
They pretty much know
what they're doing.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:07.019
Yeah, they're pros.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:11.457
-And I got to write with them,
and we did it mostly over Zoom.

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:13.426
-That's wild.
-Which was just kind of

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:17.263
deranged, honestly,
but really fun.

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.164
There were moments where --
There was a time difference.

00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:21.567
I was in Copenhagen at the time
because I'm half Danish,

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:22.801
and I was getting my citizenship

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:26.038
so I can get out of here
if I need to.

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:28.240
[ Laughter ]
Hey, you gotta plan ahead.

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:29.909
You never know.
-You gotta think ahead.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.244
-Yeah, of course.

00:03:31.244 --> 00:03:32.845
-And so I was doing that
at the time,

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:35.381
and so, often, our Zoom calls

00:03:35.381 --> 00:03:37.717
would be at like 2:00
in the morning for me.

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:39.318
And so we'd all be, like,
bundled up

00:03:39.318 --> 00:03:40.853
with our, like, blankets

00:03:40.853 --> 00:03:43.389
and our tea
and just like hammering

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.090
in every single word and line

00:03:45.090 --> 00:03:47.159
and deciding
what we wanted to say.

00:03:47.159 --> 00:03:48.694
And, like, our coping mechanism

00:03:48.694 --> 00:03:53.733
became breaking into
"Kiss By a Rose," by Seal.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.901
-That -- That would
bring you back?

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.337
Yeah.
Whenever we were like,

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.905
"Oh, this is really tough,"
we would be like,

00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:03.610
♪ Baby, I compare you to
a kiss from a rose ♪

00:04:03.610 --> 00:04:06.679
Like, that was the way that we
would just kind of defuse...

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.981
[ Both singing gibberish ]

00:04:08.981 --> 00:04:10.516
-♪ You ♪
Yeah, yeah, yeah, that's a jam.

00:04:10.516 --> 00:04:12.117
-What a song.
-Seal -- that's my jam.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:15.121
-Such a good song.
-Well, for anyone who hasn't

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.523
seen the Broadway musical
"Dear Evan Hansen,"

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.758
which again,
this is Broadway week,

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:22.228
so please buy tickets to go see
these Broadway musicals

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:26.032
that are on Broadway and support
these actors and everyone,

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:29.235
the crew and everybody,
how do we set up

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:32.638
"Dear Evan Hansen,"
and how do we set up this movie?

00:04:32.638 --> 00:04:35.908
-Sure. Well, I think
"Dear Evan Hansen"

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:39.245
hopefully addresses
a lot of kind of the ways

00:04:39.245 --> 00:04:43.449
in which we all universally
struggle with mental illness.

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:46.953
And so, hopefully, it serves
as a place for people

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.221
to feel seen and understood

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.823
when it comes to dealing
with depression and anxiety.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.325
And, you know,
all of us who are a part of it

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:55.628
have dealt with that,
are continuing to deal with that

00:04:55.628 --> 00:04:56.829
in some way, shape, or form.

00:04:56.829 --> 00:05:00.967
And the film is really
just about knowing

00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.701
that you're not alone
in that experience,

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:05.171
that it's normal to struggle,
it's normal to feel weird

00:05:05.171 --> 00:05:07.940
or deal with social anxiety.

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:10.409
And, yeah, I hope that it makes
people feel that way.

00:05:10.409 --> 00:05:13.179
-Yeah. Well, it was --
You're fantastic in the movie,

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:15.214
and you're
a really good dinner date.

00:05:15.214 --> 00:05:16.316
I loved sitting
next to you, bud.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.550
-I had a really
good time with you.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.817
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:18.817 --> 00:05:21.387
Here's Amandla Stenberg
in "Dear Evan Hansen."

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:23.188
Take a look at this.

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:25.291
-♪ You ever
look at all the people ♪

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:28.694
♪ Who seem to know
exactly how to be ♪

00:05:28.694 --> 00:05:32.064 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:32.064 --> 00:05:35.835
♪ You think they don't need
piles of prescriptions ♪

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.670
♪ To function naturally ♪

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:40.005 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:40.005 --> 00:05:43.075
♪ Well, look again,
and you might catch it ♪

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:46.379
♪ Just stay a minute more ♪

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:51.317
♪ There's this little moment
after the sunny smile ♪

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:55.988
♪ As their eyes fall
to the floor ♪

00:05:55.988 --> 00:05:59.057
♪ The anonymous ones ♪

00:05:59.057 --> 00:06:03.429
♪ Never let you see
the ache they carry ♪

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.231 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.199
-Yeah.
That's how you do it.

00:06:07.199 --> 00:06:09.602
Amandla Stenberg!

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:12.705
"Dear Evan Hansen"
is in theaters September 24th.

